  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Based on a discussion BillB, ChrisW, TimD, Asger, and others had at OR09:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Move toward having a war file for Fedora that doesn' t need to be modified.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1) Make AuthN stuff plug in via an always-configured servlet filter that delegates to what's configured",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2) Don't use Tomcat for SSL (recommend Apache for this)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "3) Make \"fedora home\" conventionally at /fedora (and don't include it in the war by default)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "There was also some discussion that needs to be further rationalized re: running multiple Fedoras in one Tomcat.  A couple ways to go:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "a) require that people edit the war file in these cases (to point to a different fedora.fcfg)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "b) have a convention where it's stored in /fedora/config/fedora-context.fcfg",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Looking at this again, I like a) because it seems to be needed anyway if people need to install in a dir that isn't /fedora (e.g. /usr/local, or whatever convention their sysadmin uses)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
